room warehouse "Harbour Loft"
  bg bg_warehouse_wide
  width 2560
  music music_office
  grade "brightness(0.95) saturate(0.85)"
  perspective horizon 250 ref 875 height 400
  # The floor only shows in a strip along the bottom: the crates, the ledger desk and the back
  # wall all meet it at y≈840, so Fenn walks in front of them.
  walk (470,875) (515,848) (2330,838) (2380,838) (2500,875)
  entry 2280,856
  arrive alley 2280,856

  # Atmosphere: a candle stub on the ledger desk, and dust in its light.
  footsteps wood
  light 1167,492 radius 160 candle
  motes dust (1130,20) (1480,0) (1900,520) (1500,600) (1250,420) count 50

  hotspot ledger "harbour ledger"
    show if not ledger_taken
    area 1210,470 270x130
    stand 1430,858
    look "The harbour ledger. The Harbourmaster's own book. Clerks keep the day-books and aren't allowed up here. Three years I've wanted one page."
    open "The Arcadia. “Lost at sea”, in Bramwick's hand, three days before she was even late."
      say "Beside it: “Quarantine dues, Gullet Key station. Paid, Cray & Co.” Nobody pays on a wreck. He wasn't writing my father off. He was paid to."
      set ledger_read
      note ledger_read "Bramwick's hand: the Arcadia, lost at sea, three days early. Beside it: “Quarantine dues, Gullet Key station. Paid, Cray & Co.”"
      sound chime
    use "The Arcadia. “Lost at sea”, in Bramwick's hand, three days before she was even late."
      say "Beside it: “Quarantine dues, Gullet Key station. Paid, Cray & Co.” Nobody pays on a wreck. He wasn't writing my father off. He was paid to."
      set ledger_read
      note ledger_read "Bramwick's hand: the Arcadia, lost at sea, three days early. Beside it: “Quarantine dues, Gullet Key station. Paid, Cray & Co.”"
      sound chime
    pull "It's chained to the desk. Of course it is."
    state if act 4
      look "The harbour ledger, still chained to its desk. The Arcadia's entry is where I left it. Lost at sea, three days early, paid by Cray & Co."
      open "I've read it. Reading it won't be enough. Cray's counting on that. The inquiry will want the book itself, and it's chained to the desk."
        nothing
      use "I've read it. Reading it won't be enough. Cray's counting on that. The inquiry will want the book itself, and it's chained to the desk."
        nothing
      pull "Chained. Bramwick chained it there himself, by regulation, so it could never go anywhere it might be embarrassed."
      pickup "It's chained to the desk. Regulation thirty-one, and a very good padlock."
    state if ledger_read = true
      name "harbour ledger"
      look "The entry still says lost. It will keep saying it until someone makes it say otherwise."

  hotspot crates "stacked crates"
    area 30,150 420x560
    nowalk
    look "More of Cray's cloud-stamped crates, stencilled for ports no ship reaches now. Somebody is paying storage on a great deal of nothing."

  hotspot stairs_down "stairs to the lane"
    area 2400,300 160x460
    stand 2360,856
    exit alley sound hatch
    look "The loft stairs, back down to the lane."

  hotspot chain "broken chain"
    show if act 4 and ledger_taken
    area 1210,470 270x130
    stand 1430,858
    look "A broken chain, and a clean oblong in the dust where the ledger sat for thirty years. Regulation thirty-one is suspended, like its author."

  use crowbar on ledger if act 4
    "I get the crowbar through the chain and lean. The staple comes out of thirty years of oak. The ledger is mine to carry."
    give ledger
    set ledger_taken
    sound pickup
